"""THE WORLD IN 24 HOURS - Wednesday 25 November 2026.

A program that draws one 1024x1024 newspaper front page summing up the
world's news of Wednesday 25 November 2026, for the make.fun bounty
news-image-20261125, entered by @badd-airdrop2.

Pure Python 3 standard library only: no network, no fonts on disk, no
randomness, no clock. Type is set from glyph bitmaps rasterised from
DejaVu (free licence) and embedded below as data; the page is drawn on
a 2x supersampled canvas with a hand-written PNG encoder and written
to /output/entry.png. Running it twice writes the same bytes.

Every story on the page happened or was first reported on Wednesday
25 November 2026, as the named outlets reported it. Stories that look
like 25 November news but are not are listed in the DATE CHECK panel
with their real dates, not presented as the day's news. Items marked
SCHEDULED were announced for later in the day; all times are UTC.
"""

